ga3W(){return"\u2022 Bachelor's program at the Dourados campus (2010 curriculum aligned with the SBC Reference Curriculum and MEC guidelines)\n\u2022 Trains professionals to plan, develop, deploy, and manage computational solutions for commercial, industrial, and scientific problems\n\u2022 Training pillars: Computing Fundamentals, Computing Technology, Mathematics, Basic Sciences, Digital Electronics, and Social & Professional Context\n\u2022 Core track includes algorithms & data structures, software engineering, databases, computer networks, operating systems, AI, compilers, computer graphics, and parallel/distributed programming\n\u2022 Theory-practice integration through labs, supervised internship, final project (TCC), and complementary activities\n\u2022 Graduate profile: industry (public/private/self-employed) or academic path toward graduate studies"},
ga3X(){return"\u2022 Lato sensu specialization in Mobile Apps and Cloud Computing (Universidade Positivo, Curitiba)\n\u2022 Mobile track: Android 1 & 2, iOS 1 & 2, Windows Phone 8 1 & 2\n\u2022 Languages: Java (Android at the time), Objective-C (iOS), and C# (Windows Phone)\n\u2022 Cloud track: Heroku, AWS, and Microsoft Azure (then also branded Windows Azure)\n\u2022 Mobile architecture patterns of the era, agile methodologies, and entrepreneurship\n\u2022 Hands-on training to ship and operate multi-platform apps with cloud-backed services"},
